  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). No common pair. Pattern: Xを{研|と}ぐ (to sharpen/wash X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing action. {研|と}いでいる = 'is sharpening/washing.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {包丁|ほうちょう}を{研|と}ぐ (to sharpen a knife)\n- {米|こめ}を{研|と}ぐ (to wash rice)\n- {砥石|といし}で{研|と}ぐ (to sharpen with a whetstone)\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n- {砥石|といし} - whetstone\n- {研|と}ぎ{器|き} - sharpener\n- {無洗米|むせんまい} - no-wash rice\n\nNOTE: The rice-washing meaning ({米|こめ}を{研|と}ぐ) is very common in everyday Japanese. Modern rice cookers often use {無洗米|むせんまい} that doesn't need washing.",
